    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d331">

                <pb facs="0553" n="507" xml:id="pg507"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.5914/56½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">7 January, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: The acquisition of the
                    Danish West Indies seems to me of sufficient importance to justify us in
                    negotiating on the basis of twenty-seven millions. I think it would be a mistake
                    to break off at this evidently opportune time on a question of money, within
                    reasonable bounds.</p>
                <p>I take it, from your letter, that your own judgment is the same.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
